& [Intent] make a future I03A host-admission attempt independently auditable and prevent delayed event queries aggregated shell exits cache reuse or UI wording from laundering a blocked build into a pass

& [BoundInputs] are exact
  + I03A Revision 1 canonical candidate 7527 bytes SHA256 E177931095AED001004C4DC56E8C2490394BBCFD208193BD1E444C63FF5F9077
  + inactive phase-lock candidate 1877 bytes SHA256 74B4E1F2BF8380915B485D8281BE78D4D22745F8F83759CD8F19211B13220EBB
  + requirement matrix 2997 bytes SHA256 AE4CC67B48BBF4CCC850FC2E72BEED2F62A285D13C4B29C8E44BA58644F0BC6E
  + activation plan 1462 bytes SHA256 DB8ECB7BB10B2913266B08CD4348363B8B0206488E7C26680F95578E7FB9F52B
  + preserved application-control fault 2840 bytes SHA256 EFFBE1A97FD7C86FD28B32190F6BB27BBA78C40DF8D3A778BCB78B1FCC4A9A23

& [PreservedBlock] is authoritative historical evidence
  + jsonschema release build helper was denied before execution at 2026-08-05T18:53:37-05:00
  + rejected path was C:\Project\Cantor\.local\cpms_i03_dependency_probe\target\release\build\icu_normalizer_data-e0e61e6bbcbd3e60\build-script-build.exe
  + Code Integrity events 3033 and 3077 named cargo.exe and Enterprise signing policy 0283ac0f-fff1-49ae-ada1-8a933130cad6
  + debug locked offline build and runtime probe passed before the release denial
  + release behavior did not execute and no release pass exists

& [CurrentRetentionObservation] explains evidence loss without rewriting history
  + read-only query observed Code Integrity Operational log enabled in Circular mode
  + maximum size was 1052672 bytes with 1200 retained records
  + oldest retained record was 444880 at 2026-08-05T20:50:58.5449894-05:00
  + newest retained record was 446079 at 2026-08-05T21:07:04.6482408-05:00
  + 596 retained events with ids 3033 3077 or 3118 in the queried four-hour interval were Chrome Vulkan or SwiftShader events
  + zero presently retained matching messages named Cantor cargo cpms_i03 or a target path
  + the 18:53 Cantor records precede the oldest retained record and have rolled out of the circular log
  + current absence therefore proves neither that the historical denial did not occur nor that a new I03A artifact would pass

& [ImmediateCaptureRule] is mandatory for any future attempt
  + capture log configuration oldest newest record ids and wall-clock boundary immediately before the command
  + execute exactly one build or test command as one process invocation
  + record its native exit code before any other command runs
  + capture all new Code Integrity records after the watermark immediately when the process returns
  + capture records by EventRecordID and time boundary in structured XML plus a normalized projection
  + bind both raw and normalized evidence by byte count and SHA256 before unrelated application events can roll them out

& [CommandIsolation] prevents aggregate-exit laundering
  + one evidence attempt contains one executable path one argument vector one working directory one environment projection and one result
  + no semicolon pipeline follow-up metadata command finally block or later successful query may determine the attempt exit disposition
  + stdout and stderr are captured separately and completely within finite limits
  + timeout cancellation launch failure and policy denial remain different terminal states
  + a wrapper fault makes the attempt indeterminate and cannot be retried silently

& [FreshTargetRule] prevents cache substitution
  + future activation uses a newly created empty explicit target directory unique to the attempt
  + exact path identity is recorded before launch
  + no prior build artifact hard link copied helper or warmed target may satisfy compilation
  + global immutable registry source cache may supply locked offline crate sources but its identity and checksums are recorded
  + fresh target remains evidence after the attempt until reviewed and is not deleted by this protocol

& [ArtifactObservation] is stage-specific
  + enumerate generated build helpers test harnesses libraries and final artifacts that exist after the attempt
  + record repository-relative or declared external path role bytes SHA256 PE machine and Authenticode disposition where applicable
  + distinguish absent not_generated generated_not_launched launched_pass launched_fail and launch_blocked
  + do not call Authenticode NotSigned a behavioral failure or a digital signature
  + do not infer helper execution from file existence or final compilation from helper creation

& [EventProjection] preserves exact attribution
  + log name provider event id EventRecordID time created process path target path policy id policy level and message digest
  + raw event XML bytes and SHA256
  + normalized projection excludes localized display prose from semantic identity when structured fields exist
  + unrelated Chrome or other application events remain separate records and cannot be attributed to Cantor
  + missing or rolled records are represented as unavailable rather than reconstructed from memory

& [AttemptDisposition] is closed
  + admitted_pass means command exit success required artifacts and tests succeeded and no new denial applies to the attempt
  + behavioral_fail means process launched and reported failure without a host launch denial
  + launch_blocked means application control denied a required process before execution
  + build_incomplete means a prerequisite stage did not produce the required successor
  + launch_fault means operating-system launch failed without sufficient policy classification
  + timed_out cancelled evidence_incomplete or wrapper_fault retain their literal meanings
  + only admitted_pass may satisfy the host-admission conjunct and it does not satisfy other I03A requirements

& [NoEventRule] is cautious
  + absence of a new denial event supports admission only when the command itself exits success and required fresh artifacts and test output are bound
  + event-log silence alone is never a pass
  + event-log rollover during the attempt makes policy evidence incomplete unless raw records were already captured

& [AuthorizedEnvironmentPaths] are alternatives not present authority
  + same workstation with artifacts that genuinely meet active Enterprise signing policy
  + organization-authorized build runner whose policy environment and custody are recorded
  + organization-authorized policy revision performed by its responsible administrator outside Cantor
  + none permits Codex to disable Smart App Control change Code Integrity policy add exclusions elevate privileges substitute binaries or self-assert signing authority

& [FutureExecutionSequence] is gated
  * verify exact preserved source canonical phase candidate requirements and baseline
  * obtain separate I03A implementation authority and form the exact four-surface diff
  * review dependency resolution source checksums features licenses build scripts proc macros native links and advisories
  * establish a fresh target and pre-command host watermark
  * run one focused locked offline debug command and immediately seal evidence
  * run one focused locked offline release command and immediately seal evidence
  * run every aggregate default and all-feature debug release format lint docs audit and evidence gate as individually attributed attempts
  * review complete evidence and issue project satisfaction plus active phase lock only if all conjuncts pass
  + a block failure missing record stale identity or scope expansion stops the sequence

& [FocusedCommandIdentity] is future exact
  + package is cantor_procedure_tool
  + test target is schema_validator_dependency
  + feature is schema-conformance
  + dependency resolution is locked and offline
  + debug and release are separate attempts
  + exact executable arguments environment and expected test inventory bind the future activation record after the four-surface diff exists

& [EvidenceBundle] is non-circular
  + AttemptCore excludes its own digest and contains command environment watermark result artifacts and events
  + compute AttemptCore digest after capture
  + ReviewEnvelope binds core digest reviewer evidence disposition predecessor and authority boundary
  + optional digital signature attaches to the envelope digest under a separately trusted key policy
  + no checksum digest review statement or project satisfaction record is called a cryptographic signature

& [FiniteLimits] precede execution
  + at most 64 attempts in one activation campaign
  + at most 4096 new event records per attempt
  + at most 4096 artifacts per attempt
  + stdout and stderr each at most 67108864 bytes
  + raw XML at most 16777216 bytes per event and total evidence at most 1073741824 bytes per attempt
  + paths at most 32768 UTF-16 code units and argument count at most 1024
  + checked arithmetic governs counts byte totals record-id ranges and allocations
  + exhaustion stops with evidence_incomplete and never truncates into a pass

& [ReviewSeparation] requires seven faculties
  + Scribe checks raw command output event and artifact custody
  + Refiner checks stage and disposition classification
  + Weaver binds command process artifact event policy and requirement relations
  + Planner checks prerequisite order stop rules and remaining gates
  + Honesty checks attribution non-erasure and claim scope
  + Security checks no bypass fresh target capability and policy boundary
  + Observer reconstructs completeness and issues only the bounded disposition

& [PresentAction] is formation only
  + no retry compile Cargo edit fresh target executable event export policy mutation signature or external message occurs
  + read-only log queries do not prove admission
  + historical Cantor denial remains the current host blocker

& [NeverAuthority] is strict
  - never: security bypass policy disablement exclusion elevation unauthorized signing binary substitution dependency activation Cargo Rust mutation compilation execution compatibility admission provider model service persistence network notification production hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [RequestedProcessing] apply Source Preservation SJS constraint extraction data design requirement support seven-faculty review plan proof inactive phase lock and narrative attribution to this exact source
